# Changelog (engine/v1/)

## Capsule `rounding` primitive option
**What:** Capsules take `primitiveOptions.rounding`, the share of each half-height taken by its cap: cap height = `rounding × y/2`, straight section = the rest, horizontal radii `x/2`/`z/2`. The mesh always fits the authored `x × y × z` box (previously the cap height was `min(x, z)/2` regardless of `y`). Payload default `0.75`, range `0.05–0.95`. The decal surface map (JS and GLSL) takes `rounding` too, through a new `u_rounding` uniform on both decal programs and the new exported `DecalRounding(shape, primitiveOptions)` (returns `rounding` for capsules, `0` otherwise). Every existing capsule carries an explicit `rounding = min(x, z)/y`, reproducing its old shape; Jeff's shorts use `0.3`.
**Where:** [NewObject.js](engine/v1/builder/NewObject.js) (`buildCapsule`, `BuildGeometry`), [Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js) (`decalSurfaceUvGLSL`, `CapsuleBand`, `DecalSurfaceUv`, `SelectDecalFacets`, `DecalRounding`, decal uniforms, scatter decal batches), [Simulator.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Simulator.js) (`buildDecalVertices`, `decalSurfaceNormal`), [canonSchemas.json](engine/v1/core/canonSchemas.json) (`capsuleOptions`), [normalize.js](engine/v1/core/normalize.js) (`normalizePart`, `normalizeLevelObject`), [characters.json](engine/v1/player/characters.json), `carlGames/simulator/json/entities.json`.

## Steep-surface grounding: launched flag, incline-scaled grip, contact grace, box face normals
**What:**
- New entity fields `launched` and `contactGrace`.
  - `launched` is set on the jump launch and on knockback. It replaces the `action === "Jumping"` grounding veto in `ResolveGrounded`, and clears once velocity·alignedUp ≤ EPSILON. `RespawnPlayer` resets it.
  - `contactGrace` is reset by `snapOrientationUpright`.
- `ApplySurfaceCorrection` removes the full surface-normal velocity while grounded and not launched; otherwise, only the into-surface component.
- New `CONFIG.PHYSICS.Correction.MinGripSpeed` (`Air`/`Water`, `0.8`). `ClassifySurface` takes a `speedRatio` (tangent speed / character `maxSpeed`; non-player entities pass `Infinity`). It demotes walkable to `"sliding"` when `speedRatio < MinGripSpeed × (cos(Ground) − normal.y) / (cos(Ground) + 1)`.
- Contact grace, 0.05 s (hardcoded `contactGraceSeconds`).
  - After an unforced contact loss, `alignedUp`, `surfaceNormal` and the whole rotation are held, and the reference-normal release waits.
  - A launch skips the grace. It ticks once per step.
- `ApplyPlayerSurfaceOrientation` always applies its pivot shift: about the ground capsule cap while in contact, about the rest-AABB centre when releasing.
- Box ground probes (`tryAABB`/`tryOBB`) report the normal of the face the probe sits furthest outside of, not the interpolated edge direction.
- Unused `DivideVector3`/`ToVector3` imports removed from Collision.js.

**Where:**
- [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js)
- [Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js) (`resetSurfaceState`, `ClassifySurface`, `ApplySurfaceCorrection`, `ApplyPlayerSurfaceOrientation`, `ResolveGrounded`)
- [Collision.js](engine/v1/physics/Collision.js) (`ProbeGroundContact`)
- [physics/Master.js](engine/v1/physics/Master.js) (`runPhysicsLoop`)
- [player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js) (`RespawnPlayer`, `snapOrientationUpright`)
- [Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js) (`UpdateMovement`)
- [Enemy.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Enemy.js)
- [config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js)

## Kept-footing pinning; void linings carry their void's id
**What:**
- `ApplySurfaceCorrection` takes `frameStart`, and removes off-surface velocity only with kept footing: grounded last step, or the contact's `surfaceId` equals the last surface stood on (`frameStart.surfaceId`).
- `physicsRuntime.groundSurfaceId` now updates only when the probe hits, so it holds the last surface through misses. `frameStart` carries it.
- Void-lining probe hits report the void's own id (e.g. `cave-tunnel`) instead of the host's.

**Where:**
- [Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js) (`ApplySurfaceCorrection`)
- [physics/Master.js](engine/v1/physics/Master.js) (`runPhysicsLoop`)
- [Collision.js](engine/v1/physics/Collision.js) (`ProbeGroundContact` → `probeVoidWalls`)

## Ramped grip demand
**What:**
- New entity field `gripDemand`, reset by `snapOrientationUpright`.
- New `CONFIG.PHYSICS.Correction.GripRampSeconds` (`2`).
- New exported `UpdateGripDemand(entity, groundContact, deltaSeconds)`, called once per step from `runPhysicsLoop`.
  - While in contact it moves `gripDemand` toward the surface's target, `max(0, MinGripSpeed × (cos(Ground) − normal.y) / (cos(Ground) + 1))`, at `MinGripSpeed / GripRampSeconds` per second, both up and down.
  - It holds while airborne.
- `ClassifySurface` takes `(speedRatio, gripDemand)` and demotes walkable to `"sliding"` only when incline > `Ground` and `speedRatio < gripDemand`. The incline curve moved from `ClassifySurface` into `UpdateGripDemand`.
- `ProbeGroundContact` passes `entity.gripDemand`.

**Where:**
- [Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js) (`UpdateGripDemand`, `ClassifySurface`)
- [physics/Master.js](engine/v1/physics/Master.js) (`runPhysicsLoop`)
- [Collision.js](engine/v1/physics/Collision.js) (`ProbeGroundContact`)
- [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js)
- [player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js) (`snapOrientationUpright`)
- [config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js)

## Grip ramp moved out of CONFIG
**What:** Removed `CONFIG.PHYSICS.Correction.GripRampSeconds`. `UpdateGripDemand` now uses a hardcoded `gripRampSeconds = 2`.
**Where:** [config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js), [Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js) (`UpdateGripDemand`).

## Tuning constants move to config.js (`GROUNDING`)
**What:**
- New rule [ENGINE_SEMANTICS.md §3](engine/v1/docs/rules/ENGINE_SEMANTICS.md), "Tuning Constants" (old §3 renumbered to §4; summary row added).
- New exported internal object `GROUNDING` (`JumpBufferSeconds`, `CoyoteSeconds`, `ContactGraceSeconds`, `GripRampSeconds`) in `config.js`, outside `API_CONFIG`. It replaces the module constants `jumpBufferSeconds`/`coyoteSeconds` and `contactGraceSeconds`/`gripRampSeconds`.

**Where:**
- [config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js)
- [Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js)
- [Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js)
- [ENGINE_SEMANTICS.md](engine/v1/docs/rules/ENGINE_SEMANTICS.md)

## Default camera: pivot clipping and rotation-safe follow
**What:**
- The orbit pivot is now clipped by a cast from the player's body centre (the `collision.aabb` midpoint) up to it, using `checkCameraObstruction`. Skipped while the Simulator is active.
- New `defaultCamRuntime.pivot`, a lagged orbit centre seeded from the initial `state.target`. The pivot lerps toward the target, the orbit direction lerps separately and is re-normalized, and the camera sits at `pivot + direction × currentDistance`. This replaces the straight-line position lerp.
- Removed the unused `MultiplyVector3` import.

**Where:** [Camera.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Camera.js) (`updateDefaultCamState`, `InitializeCameraState`)

## Default camera: obstruction on the eased direction, orbit-based input basis
**What:**
- The eased orbit direction is now computed before the obstruction check, and both the obstruction ray and the camera placement use it.
- `cameraState.forward`/`right` now come from the eased orbit direction, not from the look vector. `cameraState.up` is still built from the real look vector.

**Where:** [Camera.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Camera.js) (`updateDefaultCamState`)

## Carried heading: parallel transport between surfaces
**What:**
- New local helper `transportAcross(v, from, to)`, a minimal-rotation transport from the previous up to the current up. `advanceCarriedForward` now applies it before the yaw delta and the final projection. It reseeds instead when up flips by half a turn in one step.
- `inputFrame.previousUp` is set each `UpdateMovement` and initialised to world up.
- `Movement.js` imports `EPSILON`.

**Where:**
- [Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js) (`advanceCarriedForward`, `UpdateMovement`)
- [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js)
- [player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js) (`RespawnPlayer`)

## Ground probe: boxes ground only through a face the probe is over
**What:** `tryAABB` and `tryOBB` return a hit only when the probe is outside exactly one of the box's axes. Embedded probes (0 axes) and probes past an edge or corner (2+ axes) return null. `t` is that axis's excess, and the normal is that face's axis. This replaces the largest-excess face tiebreak.
**Where:** [Collision.js](engine/v1/physics/Collision.js) (`ProbeGroundContact`)

## Kept-footing ground reach
**What:** `runPhysicsLoop` now computes a per-step `groundReach` and passes it to `ProbeGroundContact` and `ApplyGroundSnap` in place of `groundSnapTolerance`.
- For an entity that is grounded and not `launched`: `groundSnapTolerance` + |displacement| × sin(`MaxAngleDelta[Water|Air].Ground`), with the medium chosen by `entity.underwater`.
- Otherwise: `groundSnapTolerance` alone.
- It applies to every entity that runs correction.

`Master.js` now imports `Vector3Length`.

**Where:** [physics/Master.js](engine/v1/physics/Master.js) (`runPhysicsLoop`)
